<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="
          http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
          https://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.23.xsd">

    <!--
      A phone number on the pair itself, for the one registration path that has
      no account behind it: "prijavi para" without signing in.

      Why the column has to exist at all: a signed-in registration is reachable
      — the organiser opens the submitter's profile and finds their number
      there. An anonymous one carries no profile, no email and no push token,
      so a name alone would leave the organiser with a row they cannot confirm,
      cannot chase and cannot tell apart from a scripted submission. The phone
      is therefore REQUIRED for anonymous registrations (enforced in
      SelfRegistrationService, not by a NOT NULL here — organiser-added and
      signed-in pairs legitimately have none).

      Nullable, no default and no backfill: every existing row predates the
      anonymous path and genuinely has no number.

      varchar(32) matches the DTO's @Size and is generous for the stored form
      ("+385 91 234 5678"). It is deliberately NOT unique — a household phone
      registering two pairs is normal; the (name, phone) duplicate check that
      guards against double submission lives in the service, where it can be
      case-insensitive on the name.

      PII note: this column is organiser-only on the wire. PairMapper emits it
      solely for a viewer who passes TournamentAccess.canManage, the same gate
      that already decides who sees claim tokens.

      columnExists / MARK_RAN so a database where this was added by hand is a
      no-op rather than a startup failure.
    -->

    <changeSet id="2026-09-10-pairs-contact-phone" author="mrodek">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not>
                <columnExists tableName="pairs" columnName="contact_phone"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>

        <addColumn tableName="pairs">
            <column name="contact_phone" type="varchar(32)"/>
        </addColumn>

        <rollback>
            <dropColumn tableName="pairs" columnName="contact_phone"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
